{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Minor Arp",
 "category": "80s and synth-pop leads",
 "text": "Sound: a pulsing, minor-key arpeggio, the hypnotic sequenced backbone of 80s synth-pop and soundtracks: up a minor chord and back down, sixteen notes a bar. It plays by itself.\n\nHow it's built: Clock 1/16 \u2192 Sequencer playing root, minor third, fifth, octave and back \u2192 a pulse wave through the Ladder filter; a short envelope plucks filter and VCA together; a Delay and a Reverb. Hold a key around middle C and the arpeggio plays from it (a minor chord on that note).\n\nTweak: TEMPO, the step knobs (4 instead of 3 makes it a major chord), the envelope's DECAY, the delay's FEEDBACK.",
